WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Nvidia supplies $250 million in UK compute for agentic safety research over five years. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 203. Yahoo Finance reports an annual allocation of $50 million will help British researchers strengthen safeguards for increasingly powerful AI. Jensen Huang stated that AI capability and safety must advance together. The resources will support Oxford's bold initiative, which develops approaches that help AI systems learn, adapt, and operate

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:36.320
alongside people, along with Imperial College Robotics Safety work and University College London programs.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:45.300
British AI Minister Kenishka Narayan said the donation will help ensure future AI is safe, secure, and serves people's best interests.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:52.760
The pledge follows Microsoft President Brad Smith's comments that the UK is well placed to lead AI Safety Guidelines work.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:58.720
Scrutiny of AI safety has intensified after anthropic and open AI disclosed instances

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.780
of rogue or undesired behavior by AI agents.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:08.820
Google made Gemini 4 argon generally available on the Gemini API, AI Studio, and the Gemini

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:12.200
app for developers, enterprises, scientists, and consumers.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:19.040
Mark TechPost says the sparse mixture of experts or MOE model supports up to 1 million output

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:19.500
tokens.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:23.840
It is the first model from the lab to expose that output length and production.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:28.180
It leads the Val's index at 68.90%.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:33.940
Pricing at launch stands at $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.180
The price is scheduled to double on December 1st.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:45.340
LFM 2.5 to 24bA2B arrived from Liquid AI as a 24 billion parameter on-device reasoning model,

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:48.260
with 2.45 billion active parameters.

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:55.080
the hugging-face blog details. It scores 48.09 on live claw, competitive with

00:01:55.080 --> 00:02:01.880
QN 3.6 to 35 BA3B, despite using roughly half the active parameters. The model

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:08.060
runs at 184 tokens per second on an Apple M5 max and up to 21,000 output

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:13.940
tokens per second on a single NVIDIA B300 GPU. Pre-training scaled from roughly

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:20.300
17 trillion to 33 trillion tokens, with mid-training adding 2 trillion tokens at 32,000

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:24.880
context, and 300 billion tokens at 131,000 context.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:31.320
Post-training uses five stages including multi-domain on-policy distillation and agentic

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:35.520
reinforcement learning inside harnesses such as open-claw and Hermes agent.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:41.800
The architecture retains 40 layers with 64 experts per mixture of experts block and top

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:48.660
for routing, while expanding context from 32,000 to 131,000 tokens, and vocabulary

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.840
from 65,000 to 128,000.

00:02:52.725 --> 00:02:57.705
Workday launched SANA as the default home screen that lets users request tasks in natural

00:02:57.705 --> 00:02:59.905
language, IT Pro reports.

00:03:00.425 --> 00:03:06.125
SANA orchestrates secure Workday agents for hiring, payroll, accounting, and compliance workflows.

00:03:06.665 --> 00:03:11.665
The company also released work intelligence which decomposes job roles into tasks and

00:03:11.665 --> 00:03:14.405
and identifies which can be automated versus augmented.

00:03:15.165 --> 00:03:18.665
CEO, a Neil Busry, described Sana as the new front door

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:21.445
to Workday that flips the script from hunting through menus.

00:03:22.185 --> 00:03:24.005
Autopilot agents work continuously

00:03:24.005 --> 00:03:26.105
in the background across the same domains.

00:03:26.765 --> 00:03:29.045
The platform maintains strong links to models,

00:03:29.265 --> 00:03:31.485
including anthropic clawed, while keeping

00:03:31.485 --> 00:03:33.285
an increasingly open architecture.

00:03:33.865 --> 00:03:35.945
Inside the Unified Defense CCM,

00:03:36.245 --> 00:03:38.625
short for security information and event management,

00:03:38.625 --> 00:03:42.585
Securonics introduced an agentic mesh coordinator or SAM.

00:03:43.425 --> 00:03:48.445
SAM manages specialized agents for log search, noise filtering, incident summarization,

00:03:48.745 --> 00:03:55.405
and playbook execution while requiring human validation for high impact actions, IT News Asia reports.

00:03:56.065 --> 00:04:01.985
The system presents events as narrative stories grounded in evidence to help analysts trust recommendations faster.

00:04:01.985 --> 00:04:07.145
Chief Product Officer Simon Hunt noted that the platform limits context to a specific

00:04:07.145 --> 00:04:09.585
alert or violation to avoid confusion.

00:04:10.145 --> 00:04:14.405
The architecture addresses procurement trust by operating within strict boundaries and

00:04:14.405 --> 00:04:15.965
surfacing underlying evidence.

00:04:16.365 --> 00:04:21.205
It replaces fragmented operational tools with an integrated agentic control layer that

00:04:21.205 --> 00:04:22.705
manages repetitive tasks.

00:04:23.604 --> 00:04:29.784
The local LAMA community maintains a curated list of over 280 official model context protocol,

00:04:29.784 --> 00:04:35.004
or MCP servers from product companies and actively maintain open source projects.

00:04:35.484 --> 00:04:40.884
The repo accepts pull requests for new entries and focuses only on widely used implementations.

00:04:41.304 --> 00:04:45.604
All entries come from the companies behind the products or from actively maintained open

00:04:45.604 --> 00:04:46.324
source efforts.

00:04:47.004 --> 00:04:50.764
The list is updated regularly to reflect current production grade servers.

00:04:51.828 --> 00:04:57.788
Runner lets users train a Laura adapter directly on a quantized GGUF base without PyTorch

00:04:57.788 --> 00:05:02.608
or an FP-16 parent model, according to a local LLA post.

00:05:03.128 --> 00:05:11.308
A typical run takes a Q4KM GGUF 200 train steps, Laura Rank 8, and writes out adapter.gGUF.

00:05:11.608 --> 00:05:16.588
The adapter can be served alongside the frozen base or merged into a new GGUF.

00:05:16.948 --> 00:05:21.808
The same forward pass used for training is used for inference, so the adapter matches the

00:05:21.808 --> 00:05:23.288
exact weights it will run on.

00:05:23.288 --> 00:05:28.508
When merging a four-bit adapter, the system refuses the operation unless overridden because

00:05:28.508 --> 00:05:30.428
the adapter can disappear into the weights.

00:05:31.048 --> 00:05:38.348
Heldout exact tool call scores were measured on Q1-34B-Q4KM before and after training, and

00:05:38.348 --> 00:05:43.768
the adapter can later be folded into a standalone 8-bit or better GGUF file for any runtime.

00:05:44.744 --> 00:05:49.984
During generation, the JIT-LLM engine relocates model layers and the accompanying key-value

00:05:49.984 --> 00:05:52.524
cache between GPUs in 8 milliseconds.

00:05:53.004 --> 00:06:01.964
On a dual T4 setup, LAMMA 3.23B Q4KM moves from GPU 0 to GPU 1 with zero recomputed tokens,

00:06:02.584 --> 00:06:04.504
a local LLA write-up details.

00:06:05.084 --> 00:06:10.264
The same mechanism works across CUDA and Vulkan on laptops, enabling dynamic placement

00:06:10.264 --> 00:06:11.584
without restarting the prompt.

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:16.744
The design generates kernels for whatever hardware is present and treats layers like processes

00:06:16.744 --> 00:06:18.564
that the engine can schedule and move.

00:06:18.564 --> 00:06:24.624
On a dual V100 setup with an 1800 token chat, the move takes 20 to 21 milliseconds.

00:06:25.264 --> 00:06:30.464
The approach supports models larger than single device memory and mismatched GPUs, while

00:06:30.464 --> 00:06:31.524
conversations grow.

00:06:32.597 --> 00:06:38.557
Discover AI packs 51 hands-on labs into an offline app covering neurons, gradient descent,

00:06:38.877 --> 00:06:45.477
attention, retrieval augmented generation, or RAG, agents, fine-tuning, quantization and serving.

00:06:45.477 --> 00:06:46.297
7.

00:06:46.457 --> 00:06:52.537
Several labs execute real models inside the app, including a 1.37 million parameter transformer

00:06:52.537 --> 00:06:58.157
for the attention exercise and live character-level training with slider controls, as posted

00:06:58.157 --> 00:06:59.537
to local LAMA.

00:07:00.197 --> 00:07:03.597
The app works completely offline with no account or telemetry.

00:07:04.237 --> 00:07:09.157
Labs are grouped into six sections that progress from basic concepts to advanced deployment topics.

00:07:09.717 --> 00:07:13.517
Each lab includes a short lesson readable in plain or standard mode.

00:07:13.517 --> 00:07:18.557
code. The author welcomes contributions for new interactive labs or clearer visualizations

00:07:18.557 --> 00:07:24.793
of cause and effect. Point runner at a GGUF you already keep locally this week and train

00:07:24.793 --> 00:07:30.173
a Laura adapter without installing PyTorch. Serve that adapter beside the frozen base and

00:07:30.173 --> 00:07:35.273
skip standing up a separate training stack. Open a workday trial tenant and type a hiring

00:07:35.273 --> 00:07:40.753
or payroll request in plain language to watch Santa dispatch a governed agent. Install

00:07:40.753 --> 00:07:46.333
the Discover AI app on a laptop with the network off, then run the attention lab that executes

00:07:46.333 --> 00:07:52.853
a live transformer inside the exercise. Generate a long document with Gemini 4 argon and set the

00:07:52.853 --> 00:07:58.173
same task against current clawed and GPT-6 models to compare how each handles output length.

00:07:59.116 --> 00:08:04.076
The UK AI Safety Institute is expected to expand evaluations within the next quarter

00:08:04.076 --> 00:08:10.416
using the compute allocation. Liquid AI is anticipated to ship additional open-weight reasoning models

00:08:10.416 --> 00:08:14.236
in the LFM 2.5 family, as it completes its roadmap.

00:08:14.816 --> 00:08:18.896
15 chained Android TV boxes with four gigabytes of RAM apiece

00:08:18.896 --> 00:08:22.096
are how researchers pop the hood on Pipeline Parallelism

00:08:22.096 --> 00:08:24.556
for a 26 billion parameter model.

00:08:25.116 --> 00:08:27.376
Pipeline parallelism splits a model's layers

00:08:27.376 --> 00:08:29.376
across multiple low-memory devices.

00:08:29.976 --> 00:08:32.196
Each device computes only its assigned slice

00:08:32.196 --> 00:08:35.496
and passes activations forward to the next box in the chain.

00:08:36.256 --> 00:08:38.096
Researchers placed two layers per box.

00:08:38.096 --> 00:08:43.016
15 units were chained together to hold the full 26 billion-parameter model.

00:08:43.396 --> 00:08:46.496
That fleet ran at 0.39 tokens per second.

00:08:47.076 --> 00:08:49.056
The key value cash travels with the layers.

00:08:49.676 --> 00:08:52.796
Devices can be added or removed without reencoding the prompt.

00:08:53.336 --> 00:08:58.276
Because each box holds only a fraction of the weights, total system memory stays far below

00:08:58.276 --> 00:09:00.116
what a single GPU would require.

00:09:00.736 --> 00:09:04.336
The approach trades massive latency for extreme hardware accessibility.

00:09:04.336 --> 00:09:09.176
stability, doubling time for a self-replicating agent on such a fleet would be measured in days

00:09:09.176 --> 00:09:10.056
rather than minutes.

00:09:10.776 --> 00:09:14.056
Network bandwidth between boxes is the main engineering constraint.

00:09:14.616 --> 00:09:18.616
That link becomes the bottleneck once more than a handful of devices participate.

00:09:19.316 --> 00:09:23.876
Teams facing strict air-gapped or cost-sensitive deployments should evaluate this pattern

00:09:23.876 --> 00:09:28.116
when GPU clusters are unavailable, but idle-edge hardware is plentiful.

00:09:28.696 --> 00:09:32.836
Any single box failure halts the entire pipeline until the layer is reassigned.

00:09:32.836 --> 00:09:38.349
Before we go, the coming months should bring more enterprise suites shipping agent orchestration

00:09:38.349 --> 00:09:40.069
layers in the same vein as Sana.

